WEBVTT

00:01.770 --> 00:02.870
Big Sister...

00:04.280 --> 00:05.780
Rah!

00:11.070 --> 00:12.990
We finally meet.

00:15.220 --> 00:17.490
It's been a long time.

00:17.940 --> 00:20.490
Your name is Morse now, right?

00:21.050 --> 00:22.920
Evan Bernstein.

00:24.400 --> 00:27.710
It's been ten years, right, Liese?!

00:31.200 --> 00:33.670
The white lady?

00:38.380 --> 00:41.100
Whenever you're around, it messes me up.

00:41.100 --> 00:43.770
I can't think about anything but you.

00:43.770 --> 00:47.020
Your existence alone screws with me.

00:47.020 --> 00:49.040
So die already!

00:49.760 --> 00:51.570
You did it to spite me, right?

00:51.570 --> 00:56.880
Pretending to be me and keeping House 
Bernstein afloat the last ten years.

00:56.880 --> 00:58.630
That's not true, Evan.

00:58.630 --> 00:59.270
I...

00:59.270 --> 01:01.790
I'm ending this here and now.

01:01.790 --> 01:06.330
And then, I shall reach Ākāśa!

01:06.330 --> 01:12.050
For that, I need that Kreuz!

01:12.600 --> 01:14.090
Big Sister!

01:21.120 --> 01:23.150
I'm not letting you have her.

01:44.660 --> 01:46.990
So that's how it is.

01:46.990 --> 01:49.650
You really are always,

01:49.650 --> 01:52.500
always two steps ahead of me!

01:55.360 --> 01:57.090
Maria Bradley.

01:57.090 --> 02:01.700
Since you are here, may I take that to 
mean that you have made up your mind?

02:03.420 --> 02:05.360
It's a good opportunity.

02:05.360 --> 02:06.570
Don't worry.

02:06.570 --> 02:08.970
I'm sure there is much you want to say.

02:09.560 --> 02:12.550
After that, let Ray White handle this.

02:13.160 --> 02:15.300
Ray? Why?

02:15.300 --> 02:16.240
There he is.

02:17.790 --> 02:18.950
Ray!

02:19.560 --> 02:21.150
There you are!

02:48.980 --> 02:52.730
<b>The Iceblade <b>Sorcerer
</b>Shall <b>Rule </b>the <b>World</b></b>

03:51.750 --> 03:54.960
<b>Episode 12
The Boy Who Became the World's Strongest Sorcerer Unveils Ākāśa</b>

03:56.250 --> 03:59.100
Yes. And you're the current Iceblade, right?

03:59.100 --> 04:02.570
And you are the Glutton, Paratrogo.

04:02.570 --> 04:05.350
You know me! What an honor!

04:05.350 --> 04:08.180
You're a sorcerer who eats 
other sorcerers' engrams.

04:08.450 --> 04:10.060
I became certain of that earlier.

04:11.260 --> 04:12.700
You've got me all worked up!

04:12.700 --> 04:16.070
This Iceblade will be the best treat!

04:19.230 --> 04:20.640
What the hell is this?

04:20.640 --> 04:21.580
Damn it!

04:20.740 --> 04:24.240
Can't you be quiet for a bit, 
you uncultured swine?

04:24.240 --> 04:26.610
There's something important 
I need to discuss with him.

04:26.820 --> 04:28.320
What did you say?!

04:28.320 --> 04:31.000
It's nice to meet you, Ray White.

04:31.340 --> 04:32.440
Who are you?

04:32.440 --> 04:34.180
Lieselotte Eden.

04:34.180 --> 04:36.910
Or should I say, the 
Sorcerer of Fabrication.

04:37.220 --> 04:38.380
Fabrication...

04:39.060 --> 04:40.670
So you set this all up?

04:41.040 --> 04:44.910
I think Lydia and the others 
have an inkling already.

04:44.910 --> 04:46.680
I'll keep it brief.

04:46.680 --> 04:49.630
I am going to make her overheat.

04:49.630 --> 04:52.840
Then I want you to seal it in.

04:52.840 --> 04:54.460
You already have experience with that, right?

04:54.460 --> 04:55.160
Huh?

04:55.750 --> 04:57.390
Chronos Lock.

04:57.830 --> 05:01.060
You're the only one who can do it, 
since you're resonating with her.

05:01.060 --> 05:03.890
I'm... resonating with her?

05:04.330 --> 05:05.940
You remember, don't you?

05:09.060 --> 05:11.210
If it is to save her,

05:11.210 --> 05:13.810
I am free to use any method necessary.

05:13.810 --> 05:17.000
That is what my contract with 
Bruno Bradley stipulates.

05:17.540 --> 05:21.630
Considering the risks,
you don't seem very concerned.

05:21.630 --> 05:23.880
I've got my own objective.

05:23.880 --> 05:27.090
And for that, I didn't have the 
luxury of dismissing any option.

05:28.680 --> 05:29.900
My apologies,

05:29.900 --> 05:32.330
but would you mind taking 
care of that loud buffoon?

05:34.340 --> 05:36.340
Rah!

05:37.410 --> 05:39.310
You're pissing me off.

05:41.760 --> 05:44.480
Chronos Lock, release.

05:47.700 --> 05:48.650
Here I come.

05:48.890 --> 05:53.870
I'm going to eat up every last part of you!

06:06.960 --> 06:09.590
So you can readjust on the spot, huh?!

06:09.590 --> 06:11.220
I wouldn't expect anything less.

06:18.960 --> 06:20.810
Liese...

06:21.620 --> 06:23.770
Evan, you get it, don't you?

06:23.770 --> 06:26.060
You cannot reach me.

06:26.720 --> 06:27.950
I don't care anymore!

06:28.400 --> 06:29.830
I don't care!

06:29.830 --> 06:31.370
About Eugenics...

06:31.370 --> 06:32.420
About Ākāśa...

06:32.420 --> 06:33.580
About the Kreuz...

06:33.580 --> 06:37.590
As long as I get to kill 
you with these hands!

06:37.820 --> 06:40.470
It seems my voice doesn't reach you, either.

06:41.680 --> 06:45.830
Dark Triad System, activate!

06:48.120 --> 06:51.250
I know all about that, Evan.

06:51.250 --> 06:53.100
A forbidden technique that 
stimulates the brain,

06:53.100 --> 06:55.490
thereby amplifying a human's dark side.

06:55.490 --> 07:01.470
The engram temporarily grows 
and causes an overheat.

07:03.470 --> 07:05.770
Die!

07:09.280 --> 07:11.020
What is this?!

07:11.020 --> 07:12.650
Prima materia encoding;

07:12.650 --> 07:15.290
material code, material code, decoding,

07:13.390 --> 07:15.730
material code, processing, synesthesia,

07:15.130 --> 07:17.030
embodiment, phenomenon.

07:17.030 --> 07:18.670
Apotheosis.

07:23.920 --> 07:28.800
The destructive factor I possess is 
making your engram self-destruct.

07:29.330 --> 07:31.330
It's over, Evan.

07:33.800 --> 07:36.920
Liese!

07:43.060 --> 07:46.160
Is this... the power of the strongest...?

07:46.160 --> 07:49.570
The Sorcerer of Fabrication?

07:50.720 --> 07:52.000
No.

07:52.000 --> 07:53.800
The strongest is the Iceblade.

07:54.250 --> 07:56.780
Ray White is of another caliber.

07:56.780 --> 07:59.820
He exists in a whole different
dimension, you could say.

08:00.080 --> 08:01.710
What?

08:01.710 --> 08:05.460
Suppose there was a sorcerer who 
could rule the entire world.

08:07.080 --> 08:09.690
The only one who could do that... is him.

08:11.140 --> 08:12.530
In other words...

08:13.060 --> 08:17.010
The Iceblade Sorcerer shall rule the world.

08:17.010 --> 08:20.020
<b>The Iceblade <b>Sorcerer
</b>Shall <b>Rule </b>the <b>World</b></b>

08:24.980 --> 08:26.790
Is it all... over?

08:26.790 --> 08:28.560
I can't take this anymore!

08:30.030 --> 08:31.480
We did it!

08:31.480 --> 08:34.930
Even though we couldn't do a single 
thing in the Kafka Forest exercise.

08:34.930 --> 08:37.410
That shows how far all of us have come.

08:37.410 --> 08:39.580
And all because of Ray, huh?

08:39.580 --> 08:40.470
Yeah.

08:40.470 --> 08:43.240
We'd never have come this 
far if it wasn't for him.

08:44.110 --> 08:46.570
Especially you, Albert.

08:46.570 --> 08:47.500
Right?

08:47.500 --> 08:48.690
Right.

08:53.510 --> 08:54.590
This can't be...

08:54.590 --> 08:55.810
That's...

08:55.810 --> 08:57.710
The same thing as in Kafka Forest?!

09:00.180 --> 09:01.400
Run!

09:01.760 --> 09:03.040
Damn it!

09:06.020 --> 09:06.990
What the...

09:08.350 --> 09:10.640
You all did great!

09:11.230 --> 09:12.830
Sorry we kept you waiting.

09:13.270 --> 09:16.370
You were fighting in your outfits, too!

09:16.640 --> 09:19.300
You're getting top points for this.

09:18.570 --> 09:20.780
We'll be taking it from here.

09:24.630 --> 09:26.620
Let's get rid of the last ones.

09:26.620 --> 09:27.460
The last ones?

09:27.460 --> 09:28.190
What do you mean?

09:28.190 --> 09:29.470
Sorry about that!

09:29.470 --> 09:32.800
These guys were actually all over.

09:32.800 --> 09:36.560
Streams of men who hit on you 
and bugs are so annoying.

09:37.880 --> 09:39.600
So ridiculous...

09:39.980 --> 09:42.280
Those seven grand sorcerers...

09:45.960 --> 09:47.060
Right, then.

09:47.060 --> 09:49.490
Let's go, guys!

09:49.490 --> 09:51.600
Carocaro isn't a guy, though.

09:51.600 --> 09:52.540
Yeah, yeah.

09:58.230 --> 09:59.860
Flash of Lightning!

10:03.520 --> 10:07.050
That one is called Lightning Slash.

10:17.020 --> 10:18.500
Febris Draco!

10:19.000 --> 10:20.750
Yamata Orochi!

10:27.030 --> 10:28.750
Is that for real?

10:28.750 --> 10:30.330
I think so.

10:30.330 --> 10:31.380
So it's real, huh?

10:32.020 --> 10:33.370
Right, then!

10:33.370 --> 10:36.020
Can't be losing to my students.

10:36.020 --> 10:38.030
Carol in Wonderland,

10:38.030 --> 10:39.700
Through the Looking Glass!

10:40.090 --> 10:42.540
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go!

10:45.440 --> 10:47.760
We've finally reached the end.

10:48.180 --> 10:52.110
I'm really sad that I have 
to say goodbye today,

10:52.110 --> 10:56.960
but Carocaro promises to not forget 
all my fans until the day I forget!

10:58.250 --> 11:01.360
Now, please listen to my last song!

11:01.360 --> 11:02.090
Loud-

11:05.640 --> 11:06.850
Kyapi!

11:07.110 --> 11:09.360
What do they mean by "the end"?

11:09.600 --> 11:12.150
You all better get ready!

11:12.440 --> 11:14.100
Icicle Blades!

11:14.540 --> 11:15.730
Ragnarok!

11:17.260 --> 11:20.960
Eat this supreme sorcery!

11:26.150 --> 11:28.720
Jeez. Talk about overkill.

11:28.990 --> 11:32.190
Lydia, you're as violent as ever.

11:31.450 --> 11:33.160
I don't want to hear it from you guys.

11:33.160 --> 11:36.370
I did properly take the surrounding 
area into consideration.

11:36.370 --> 11:37.950
As if, you arsonist...

11:37.950 --> 11:40.500
My stage appearance was so moving.

11:38.770 --> 11:39.580
Well...

11:39.580 --> 11:40.680
I have no words.

11:40.680 --> 11:41.670
Wow...

11:41.670 --> 11:44.260
So, Elisa, why are you crying?

11:44.260 --> 11:46.490
Lydia's live sorcery...

11:46.490 --> 11:48.810
As an Ainser, I've been so blessed.

11:49.610 --> 11:50.500
Ray...

11:51.520 --> 11:53.360
Now it's up to you.

11:53.830 --> 11:55.810
Is this all the Iceblade can do?!

11:56.050 --> 11:57.300
Enough talk.

11:57.300 --> 11:58.560
Come at me in earnest now.

11:58.890 --> 12:02.470
Then I won't hold back anymore!

12:02.470 --> 12:04.400
This is my full power!

12:04.660 --> 12:09.200
My original spell that provides 
the ultimate body enhancement!

12:12.830 --> 12:15.280
Man-eater!

12:17.800 --> 12:18.990
Ray!

12:19.820 --> 12:21.830
This is your fault.

12:21.830 --> 12:22.770
What?

12:22.770 --> 12:26.730
This is all because you couldn't 
open your damn mouth!

12:28.230 --> 12:30.110
The fact that Ray's in that situation,

12:30.110 --> 12:32.400
that I'm like this,

12:32.400 --> 12:34.030
this entire situation!

12:34.030 --> 12:36.880
All because you never talk 
about the important things!

12:43.980 --> 12:46.490
I think it's time to eat you now!

12:50.980 --> 12:51.830
Ray!

12:54.910 --> 12:59.420
I'm going to savor you, Iceblade!

12:59.680 --> 13:01.010
Prima materia, encoding,

13:00.510 --> 13:01.970
material code, decoding,

13:01.470 --> 13:03.120
processing, deceleration,

13:02.430 --> 13:03.290
lock,

13:02.760 --> 13:04.100
restoration, compression,

13:03.320 --> 13:04.500
embodiment, picnogram,

13:04.500 --> 13:05.310
material.

13:05.310 --> 13:06.450
What's that?

13:06.450 --> 13:08.750
You want me to crush that, too?

13:11.830 --> 13:12.850
What?

13:12.850 --> 13:14.310
You bastard!

13:16.290 --> 13:19.520
That really hurts!

13:23.710 --> 13:24.870
What?

13:25.280 --> 13:27.280
It didn't break?!

13:28.810 --> 13:30.860
It's over, Paratrogo.

13:31.160 --> 13:32.420
Pandora!

13:36.070 --> 13:37.900
I see.

13:37.900 --> 13:42.140
Now I understand what you are.

13:42.140 --> 13:46.640
Iceblade, you're awesome!

13:52.320 --> 13:55.650
Chronos Lock, activate.

13:58.950 --> 13:59.870
Ray!

14:01.220 --> 14:02.370
Maria...

14:02.370 --> 14:04.550
Let me go. I need to help him.

14:04.550 --> 14:06.160
I told you this is all your fault!

14:06.520 --> 14:08.690
That's like you, always 
playing the good girl!

14:08.690 --> 14:11.030
You have it so easy, 
not knowing how others feel!

14:11.510 --> 14:12.820
Must be nice.

14:12.820 --> 14:14.580
You stay quiet and look sad,

14:14.580 --> 14:16.910
then everybody around you gets you.

14:17.700 --> 14:19.140
You...

14:21.930 --> 14:23.130
You...

14:23.890 --> 14:27.530
You have no idea what I've been through!

14:27.530 --> 14:31.300
I've suffered so much for you, as well!

14:32.970 --> 14:34.440
You idiot!

14:34.440 --> 14:36.550
You just did that on your own!

14:36.550 --> 14:38.230
I never asked you for any of that!

14:38.230 --> 14:40.800
Because you're always so needlessly caring,

14:40.800 --> 14:44.310
I always get compared to 
my wonderful older sister!

14:44.310 --> 14:46.440
And I'm just the failure of a sister!

14:48.550 --> 14:51.720
I have no choice but to always bear it!

14:51.720 --> 14:53.440
Now, and forever!

14:53.440 --> 14:54.760
Why?!

14:54.760 --> 14:57.510
If you're going to be mopey because 
you pity me, just cut it out!

14:57.510 --> 14:58.200
It's annoying!

14:58.200 --> 14:59.410
Shut up!

15:00.430 --> 15:02.650
Shut up, shut up!

15:02.650 --> 15:04.550
That's why I hate you.

15:04.550 --> 15:05.510
I hate you!

15:06.110 --> 15:08.140
Pretending to be some heroine in a drama.

15:08.140 --> 15:11.030
You rebel against our parents 
and do whatever you want!

15:11.030 --> 15:12.840
I despise you so much, Maria!

15:14.420 --> 15:16.290
Then just say so from the beginning!

15:16.290 --> 15:17.940
That I should disappear!

15:17.940 --> 15:19.780
That you don't need me.

15:19.780 --> 15:21.950
That you wish I'd never been born.

15:25.250 --> 15:27.330
Why would you say that?

15:28.070 --> 15:31.690
I've never wished you hadn't been born.

15:32.430 --> 15:34.670
There're things I don't like about you,

15:34.670 --> 15:36.580
but you are my precious little sister.

15:37.730 --> 15:39.160
I love you.

15:42.690 --> 15:43.980
Big Sister...

15:45.550 --> 15:49.310
Don't say that!

15:55.290 --> 15:57.360
Big Sister! Big Sister!

15:57.360 --> 15:58.930
Maria...

16:00.270 --> 16:01.340
Big Sister!

16:15.620 --> 16:17.850
Was he important to you?

16:18.830 --> 16:19.840
Who knows?

16:20.240 --> 16:23.080
He was seduced by a demon and got jealous.

16:23.080 --> 16:25.090
He had thrown away his humanity.

16:25.090 --> 16:26.630
A foolish man.

16:29.050 --> 16:31.390
Things don't go the way you want.

16:31.390 --> 16:33.670
In reality, that is.

16:35.930 --> 16:38.090
Hurry. Go to her.

16:40.320 --> 16:41.720
What is that?

16:41.720 --> 16:42.740
That's...

16:42.740 --> 16:44.020
Get back!

16:44.640 --> 16:46.970
The overheating is starting.

16:53.130 --> 16:56.140
Maria, stand back and wait.

16:56.480 --> 16:59.040
Please help her.

16:59.040 --> 16:59.840
I will.

17:02.010 --> 17:02.980
Miss Rebecca...

17:05.290 --> 17:10.400
Ray, I said such horrible things to Maria.

17:11.420 --> 17:13.960
You must be so disillusioned with me.

17:13.960 --> 17:14.880
No.

17:16.360 --> 17:20.190
Nobody is free of conflict or worries.

17:20.560 --> 17:23.640
I have so much respect for you.

17:23.850 --> 17:25.090
And...

17:25.090 --> 17:27.630
Maria loves you, too.

17:28.090 --> 17:29.380
Ray...

17:52.200 --> 17:53.670
Chronos Lock.

18:04.580 --> 18:07.470
So both my daughters,

18:07.470 --> 18:10.090
Rebecca and Maria, are safe.

18:10.090 --> 18:10.900
Yes.

18:11.430 --> 18:14.480
The Iceblade, Ray, was the one who did it.

18:15.010 --> 18:18.510
Could you please convey to him my gratitude?

18:28.000 --> 18:29.140
Ray!

18:29.970 --> 18:33.590
Sorry it's me, and not Ray.

18:33.590 --> 18:35.240
Oh, not at all.

18:35.700 --> 18:40.000
But it's almost time for me and Ray to...

18:40.000 --> 18:40.640
Huh?

18:40.640 --> 18:43.720
Wow, you two sure are close.

18:44.070 --> 18:45.560
Not at all.

18:45.560 --> 18:48.480
I'm still not on the same level as you.

18:48.480 --> 18:51.630
Oh, there's no need for modesty.

18:51.630 --> 18:55.940
I'm sorry, but we plan on 
spending the night together.

18:55.940 --> 18:56.370
What?

18:56.600 --> 18:58.350
You're just watching fireworks, right?

18:58.350 --> 18:59.480
Oh, no.

18:59.730 --> 19:02.340
I need to properly thank him for today.

19:02.340 --> 19:05.970
I... I showed him my gratitude, 
too, after the Magic Chevalier!

19:05.970 --> 19:09.930
And he held me tight and he told me 
he wanted us to always be together!

19:09.930 --> 19:11.430
I see, I see.

19:11.430 --> 19:14.500
Well, that sounds like a 
wonderful friendship.

19:14.500 --> 19:17.590
But my life is now forever tied to his.

19:17.820 --> 19:21.060
It wouldn't be incorrect to say that 
our souls are bound to each other.

19:21.060 --> 19:22.700
You're going to have a hard time.

19:22.700 --> 19:24.180
Ray is very popular with girls.

19:24.180 --> 19:25.070
Quite.

19:25.070 --> 19:27.650
And I do have the capacity 
to accept that fact.

19:28.040 --> 19:30.240
In the end, love always wins.

19:36.020 --> 19:37.360
I won't lose.

19:38.590 --> 19:40.000
Neither will I.

19:40.000 --> 19:42.070
You might not think it, but I hate losing.

19:43.010 --> 19:46.130
Why do you two get to have all the fun?

19:47.140 --> 19:47.940
Unfair.

19:47.940 --> 19:49.300
Huh? Hey, what?!

19:51.280 --> 19:54.160
I do have the capacity.

19:54.160 --> 19:55.940
I'm sorry I kept you waiting.

19:57.000 --> 19:58.790
You're all here?

19:58.790 --> 19:59.920
Ray!

19:59.920 --> 20:00.700
Ray!

20:00.700 --> 20:01.720
Ray!

20:01.720 --> 20:02.570
Ray!

20:12.670 --> 20:14.640
It's been a while, Howard.

20:15.010 --> 20:17.460
I'm a student now.

20:17.460 --> 20:18.800
Can you even imagine?

20:18.800 --> 20:20.650
Me, a student.

20:21.830 --> 20:25.100
After having taken so 
many lives in the war,

20:25.100 --> 20:28.500
I never thought I would 
have the right to be one.

20:29.040 --> 20:32.380
After I lost you back then,

20:32.380 --> 20:34.320
I felt so adrift.

20:35.260 --> 20:39.760
I was so stained in blood that I had 
no idea where I could ever fit in.

20:41.180 --> 20:45.270
And it was my master 
who showed me the way.

20:46.440 --> 20:52.340
The world that was normal to me was 
completely detached from the real world.

20:52.820 --> 20:54.090
Even then,

20:54.090 --> 20:57.680
there were many people who were willing 
to accept someone like me anyway.

21:00.090 --> 21:01.190
Howard,

21:02.480 --> 21:05.460
I have friends now!

21:08.240 --> 21:11.200
Amelia Rose
Saeki Iori

21:11.750 --> 21:14.710
Rebecca Bradley
Waki Azumi

21:13.140 --> 21:15.740
You can be happy now, Lydia.

21:15.250 --> 21:18.210
Elisa Griffith 
Harumura Nana

21:15.740 --> 21:18.200
Isn't that the Ray you wanted to see?

21:18.670 --> 21:19.570
Yeah.

21:18.750 --> 21:21.710
Claris Cleveland 
Hondo Kaede

21:21.080 --> 21:23.610
Lydia's crying!

21:22.260 --> 21:25.220
Evi Armstrong 
